[
 {
  "comment": "Wet Into Wet at radius 16 in black on white paper, two strokes of the harness's pen, each `move` carrying a pressure and a tilt so the brush reads a pen as it reads a tablet. The first is drawn at a steady light 0.3, the second presses at 1.0 and lightens to 0.3 over 30 moves. The `look` pictures are the composite at one document pixel a pixel, whose darkness the record reads as coverage over the first 20 pixels of each stroke and the 20 after. A `wait` after a `press` holds nothing: the harness's press reaches the brush only with the next pointer event, so the pen that rests on its press past PRESS_WAIT_MS is played by the module's suite `test_a_noise_stroke_s_first_dab_lays_no_more_paint_than_the_body_after_it.gd`."
